response.text:
I have fixed the bug in `parse-range.mjs` where parsing a single number (e.g., `"7"`) resulted in `to: NaN` instead of the number itself. I updated the logic to check if the `to` value is undefined after splitting the input string and, if so, set it equal to the `from` value.

```javascript
export function parseRange(text) {
  const [from, to] = text.split("-");
  const fromNum = Number(from);
  return { from: fromNum, to: to === undefined ? fromNum : Number(to) };
}
```
